# Copy to .env and fill in the real values. .env is gitignored; this file is not.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The Go binaries do not read .env themselves. Export it into your shell first:
#
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#   ./bin/dor run --agents=all
#
# Everything else (Postgres, TEI, NATS, gateway) has local defaults that match
# `make dev`, so only the keys below are needed for a live run.

# --- jev (TypeSafe decision model) ------------------------------------------
# A TYPESAFE_API_KEY calls https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone (jev-1.14.0).
# DOR_JEV_API_KEY or OPENROUTER_API_KEY, if set, win and go to OpenRouter.
# Endpoints, model pins and prices are in config/models.yaml.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=your-typesafe-api-key-here
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# --- Claude features (enricher fallback, briefs, "why") ---------------------
# Fallback order, comma-separated: api, claude-cli, codex-cli.
#   api        ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (pay per token)
#   claude-cli `claude -p` on your Claude subscription (run `claude` once to log in)
#   codex-cli  `codex exec` on your ChatGPT subscription (run `codex login`)
# Unset means "api" when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, and no Claude features otherwise.
DOR_LLM_BACKENDS=claude-cli,codex-cli
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Codex models for the Haiku and Opus tiers (must be allowed on a ChatGPT login).
# DOR_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
# DOR_CODEX_OPUS_MODEL=gpt-6-sol
# CLI processes in flight per backend.
# DOR_LLM_CLI_CONCURRENCY=2

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact string sent with feed fetches; some publishers block anonymous agents.
# DOR_HTTP_USER_AGENT=dor/0.1 (+mailto:you@example.com)
# Enables the ReliefWeb source. The API rejects unapproved appnames.
# DOR_RELIEFWEB_APPNAME=
